Z||000000||wxxo||06-06-2000||02:38 PM||||ok heres the deal. i ve got an 86se v6 4spd. it likes to kick out of fourth gear right after i shift into it. it only does this sometimes and i can shift into fourth after it does it. it seems to help if i shift after 3500rpms. i changed the tranny fluid as per the hanes manual and that seemed to help a little but it still happens at least once a day. thinking this is a really bad thing. what do yall think???||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||06-06-2000||05:31 PM||||There's excessive clearance somewhere (wear) or something's broken. I don't know much about the manuals in these cars, but in my old truck (three on the tree) a missing snap ring or loose transmission bolts/mounts can do this.<P>And it only happens in high gear.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||06-06-2000||05:33 PM||||Oh...could also be miadjusted linkage...not shifting completely into fourth.<P>Someone else will have to tell you how to adjust this if this is the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DiggityDan||06-07-2000||01:07 AM||||May be fourth gear synchro or shifting fork wear or cable like was mentioned earlier. If you can get it in gear, I'll bet it will be one of the first two. If you ride around with your hand on the shifter, sometimes this puts enough pressure on fourth gear to wear a few things out. When you say it pops out only at lower speeds, this makes me think synchro. Synchros will usually hold at higher RPMS.<BR>Either way you will probably have to split the case to find out for sure.||||reg||1
